cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the code, simulation outputs, or figures from this repository, please cite this research software using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "ALS Regime Switching Attrition: Functional and Respiratory Reserve Modeling"
authors:
  - name: "Prihantini"
repository-code: "https://github.com/TitinPrihantini4/als-regime-switching-attrition"
url: "https://github.com/TitinPrihantini4/als-regime-switching-attrition"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Research code and reproducible numerical outputs accompanying the manuscript
  "Regime Switching Model of ALSFRS-R Attrition and Respiratory Reserve
  Delineates Homeostatic Tipping Boundaries in Amyotrophic Lateral Sclerosis".
  The literature-parameterized mathematical proof-of-concept combines a
  four-state nonlinear ordinary differential equation model of functional
  reserve, respiratory reserve, latent disease momentum, and homeostatic
  reserve with a model-defined compensation margin. The repository includes
  scenario simulations, first-passage and boundary analyses, Latin hypercube
  sensitivity analysis, stochastic perturbations, latent-subsystem stability,
  synthetic model comparisons, and figures. No patient-level clinical
  calibration or external validation is claimed.
keywords:
  - amyotrophic lateral sclerosis
  - ALSFRS-R
  - respiratory reserve
  - nonlinear ordinary differential equations
  - first-passage analysis
  - regime classification
  - global sensitivity analysis
  - reproducible research
